course: dictionary
lesson: 12746
title: Words for people from a place
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words that name a person end in -er: a teacher teaches, a baker bakes. A Dubliner is a person from a place. It comes from Dublin, the capital city of Ireland, and means someone who is from Dublin or lives there.
explain: Look at the clues in the sentence. «She was born in Dublin, so she is a true Dubliner.» Born in Dublin tells you the meaning. Try it: swap in "a person from Dublin" and the sentence still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
explain: Dubliner has a capital D because it is a name for a person from a particular place. The same word can also be the title of a famous book. «Liam read Dubliners, a book of short stories.» Here the sentence tells you it is a book, not a person, so always check the clues.
fact: A Dubliner is a person from Dublin, the capital city of Ireland, or someone who lives there.
fact: Dublin is written with a capital D, and so is Dubliner, because it names a place and a person from that place.
fact: «Dubliners» is a book of short stories by James Joyce, first published in 1914.
fact: «Dubliners» is also the name of an Irish folk band, The Dubliners.
fact: Use the sentence around the word to decide: is it a person, or is it a book or band name?
exercise: «Maeve was born in Dublin and has lived there all her life.» What is Maeve? | A Glaswegian | A Londoner | An Australian | *A Dubliner
exercise: «Liam read Dubliners, a book of short stories.» In this sentence, what is Dubliners? | A person from Dublin | A city in France | *A book | A kind of Irish bread
exercise: «Mrs Walsh is a Dubliner who loves walking beside the River Liffey.» Find and copy one word that names a person from Dublin. | Liffey | *Dubliner | Ireland | river
test: «Our new neighbour is a Dubliner.» What does Dubliner mean? | Someone who writes songs for a living | *Someone from Dublin or who lives there | Someone who lives in a village in the countryside | A type of farm animal
test: Which word means the capital city of Ireland? | Belfast | Galway | Cork | *Dublin
exam: «Aoife is a true Dubliner.» What does this tell us about Aoife? | She has never left her house | *She comes from Dublin or lives there | She is a famous writer of books | She comes from Paris
